# Line endings are decided here, not by each machine's core.autocrlf.
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true, so a checkout writes CRLF
# while Prettier writes LF. Every `make format` then left the tree dirty with
# files whose content diff was empty — pure line-ending churn that had to be
# stepped around on each commit. Checking out LF matches what the formatter
# produces, so the two stop fighting, on every machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe can mis-parse a batch file that arrives with LF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
